---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const post = {
  title: "Esquare Estates Commonwealth: A Premium Townhouse Inside Quezon City's Most Secure Village",
  description: "Discover Esquare Estates Commonwealth — an exclusive two-unit, 4-bedroom modern contemporary townhouse by Metrostar Realty inside Ciudad Regina, Quezon City. Priced for serious buyers.",
  pubDate: new Date("2026-06-06"),
  author: "Esquare Estates",
  tags: ["quezon city", "townhouse", "investment", "premium"],
};

const formattedDate = post.pubDate.toLocaleDateString("en-PH", {
  year: "numeric",
  month: "long",
  day: "numeric",
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${post.title} | Esquare Estates`}
  description={post.description}
  activeNav="blog"
>
  <div class="blog-post">
    <header class="blog-post-header">
      <span class="eyebrow"><a href="/blog/" style="color:inherit">Blog</a></span>
      <h1>{post.title}</h1>
      <div class="blog-post-meta">
        <span><i class="fas fa-calendar-alt"></i> {formattedDate}</span>
        <span><i class="fas fa-user"></i> {post.author}</span>
        {post.tags.map((tag) => (
          <span style="background:var(--gold-100);color:var(--gold-600);padding:3px 10px;border-radius:20px;font-weight:600;font-size:.78rem">
            {tag}
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="blog-content">

      <p>
        When most people think of Esquare Estates, they think of Bulacan — flood-free lots, McArthur
        Highway, the Philippine Arena corridor. But the brand's roots go deeper. <strong>Esquare Estates
        Commonwealth</strong>, developed by <strong>Metrostar Realty &amp; Development Inc.</strong>, is a
        premium townhouse project tucked inside one of Quezon City's most established private villages:
        <strong>Ciudad Regina</strong>.
      </p>

      <p>
        This is not a mass-market development. There are only two units. And that exclusivity is exactly
        the point.
      </p>

      <h2>What Is Esquare Estates Commonwealth?</h2>

      <p>
        Commonwealth is an intimate, two-unit enclave of <strong>modern contemporary townhouses</strong>
        designed with a sleek minimalist aesthetic — clean lines, a refined palette of light hues, and a
        layout built for how Filipinos actually live. Two floors, four bedrooms, four toilets and baths,
        and a two-car carport per unit.
      </p>

      <p>
        The architecture avoids the boxy, cookie-cutter look that dominates most Philippine townhouse
        developments. Instead, the façade reads more like a premium residential design you'd see in
        BGC or Alabang — sharp angles, exposed concrete accents, full-height windows, and a deliberate
        restraint that signals quality without shouting it.
      </p>

      <h2>The Location Advantage: Ciudad Regina, Quezon City</h2>

      <p>
        Real estate value starts and ends with location, and Ciudad Regina punches well above its
        price point. It's a <strong>secure, gated village</strong> in Quezon City — not a converted
        subdivision, not a barangay road development. The project sits within a private village,
        which means controlled access, a quieter environment, and the kind of address that holds
        its value regardless of what's happening in the broader market.
      </p>

      <p>
        The connectivity from here is genuinely strong. Within roughly 20 to 25 minutes, you can
        reach <strong>Ever Gotesco</strong> and <strong>UP Town Center</strong>. SM North EDSA is
        about 31 minutes away, SM Fairview around 39. For medical needs, Diliman Doctors Hospital
        is approximately 44 minutes, with FEU-NRMF Medical Center and New Era General Hospital both
        within an hour. Schools like Diliman Preparatory School (Commonwealth Campus) are about
        32 minutes away, with School of the Holy Spirit in Quezon City at around 44 minutes.
      </p>

      <p>
        These aren't walking distances — but they are everyday-functional distances for a family
        living in a private village in the north of the metro.
      </p>

      <h2>What You Get: Unit Specifications</h2>

      <p>
        Both Unit 1 and Unit 2 share identical specifications, which matters for resale parity and
        community uniformity. Here's what each unit delivers:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Lot Area:</strong> ±150 sq. m.</li>
        <li><strong>Total Gross Floor Area:</strong> ±245.25 sq. m.</li>
        <li><strong>Enclosed Floor Area:</strong> ±152.83 sq. m.</li>
        <li><strong>Ground Floor:</strong> ±81.50 sq. m. | <strong>Second Floor:</strong> ±90.55 sq. m.</li>
        <li><strong>Bedrooms:</strong> 4 | <strong>Toilets &amp; Baths:</strong> 4</li>
        <li><strong>Carport:</strong> 2 cars (±32.77 sq. m.)</li>
        <li><strong>Floors:</strong> 2</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Home amenities include a porch, patio, kitchen, dining area, living area, and a balcony.
        There's also a maid's room with its own toilet and bath on the ground floor, a service area,
        a linear garden running alongside the unit, and a master bedroom suite on the second floor
        with a walk-in closet, workspace nook, and a lounge area by the window.
      </p>

      <p>
        For buyers who need more land — perhaps planning to expand the garden or add outdoor space —
        there's also an <strong>Option 2 variant for Unit 1</strong> with a larger lot area of
        ±300 sq. m. and total gross floor area of ±395.25 sq. m., while maintaining the same
        interior floor plan.
      </p>

      <h2>Material Specifications Worth Noting</h2>

      <p>
        Premium developments are defined as much by what's inside the walls as what's visible in
        the renders. Esquare Estates Commonwealth specifies materials that are meaningfully above
        the typical mid-market standard:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Ground floor living areas finished in <strong>glazed floor tiles</strong>; second floor bedrooms in <strong>wood plank floor tiles</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Quartz stone kitchen countertop</strong> with stainless sink and modular cabinetry including a cooktop and rangehood</li>
        <li>Master T&amp;B features a <strong>tempered glass shower partition</strong>, rainshower and telephone shower set, and a vanity with basin-type lavatory</li>
        <li><strong>Steel door with smart lock</strong> for the main entrance</li>
        <li><strong>Smart home system</strong> provision and <strong>solar power ready</strong> infrastructure</li>
        <li>Split-type ACU provisions and water heater provisions in all T&amp;Bs</li>
        <li>Reinforced concrete structure throughout, with waterproofed T&amp;B slabs</li>
        <li>Pre-painted long span roofing on steel frame with PE foam insulation</li>
        <li>Underground electrical and auxiliary lines at the project level</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        The combination of quartz countertops, smart lock entry, solar-ready wiring, and smart home
        system provision puts this well above the specifications you'd find in a comparable-price
        condominium unit — and you own the land.
      </p>

      <h2>Why Two Units Is a Feature, Not a Limitation</h2>

      <p>
        In a typical subdivision, you share a village with hundreds — sometimes thousands — of other
        families. At Esquare Estates Commonwealth, you share a community with exactly one other
        household. That means less foot traffic, less noise, a shared gate that actually functions as
        a gate, and a genuine sense of privacy that most gated communities only promise.
      </p>

      <p>
        For buyers who want the security and prestige of a village address without sacrificing privacy,
        this kind of micro-enclave is increasingly rare in Metro Manila. It's the reason developers
        who build two-unit or four-unit projects in established villages command premiums over
        standard subdivision product — and why that premium tends to hold.
      </p>

      <h2>Who Is This For?</h2>

      <p>
        Esquare Estates Commonwealth is positioned for a specific buyer — someone who:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Wants a <strong>Metro Manila address</strong> (Quezon City, not a province) in a private village</li>
        <li>Needs a <strong>4-bedroom, multi-toilet home</strong> that can accommodate a multi-generational household or frequent guests</li>
        <li>Values <strong>design quality and material finish</strong> over sheer unit count</li>
        <li>Prioritizes <strong>exclusivity and privacy</strong> — not living in a community of 500 households</li>
        <li>Sees the <strong>land ownership</strong> component as a long-term wealth asset separate from the structure</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        It's also a compelling option for <strong>OFW families</strong> who want a premium, low-maintenance
        Metro Manila home ready for occupancy — or for investors who understand that scarcity in real
        estate (two units, gated village, central QC location) is one of the most durable drivers of
        value appreciation.
      </p>

      <h2>The Bottom Line</h2>

      <p>
        Esquare Estates Commonwealth isn't trying to compete with mass-market townhouses on price per
        square meter. It's competing on a different axis entirely: <strong>address, exclusivity, and
        finish quality</strong>. Two units. A private village in Quezon City. Four bedrooms and four
        baths. Smart home system. Quartz stone counters. Solar-ready.
      </p>

      <p>
        There are a lot of townhouses in Metro Manila. There aren't many like this.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you're interested in learning more about Esquare Estates Commonwealth — including pricing,
        availability, and payment terms — get in touch with our team.
      </p>

    </div>

    <!-- CTA inside every blog post -->
    <div class="blog-cta">
      <h3>Interested in Esquare Estates Commonwealth?</h3>
      <p>Get full pricing details, floor plans, and payment terms from a property specialist.</p>
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Inquire now <i class="fas fa-arrow-right arr"></i></a>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:center;margin-top:32px">
      <a href="/blog/" class="btn-link">
        <i class="fas fa-arrow-left" style="transform:scaleX(-1)"></i> Back to all posts
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
